# Fixed defect 131's class, 2026-09-29, one missing `]` in a literal, beside
# `fixedbugs-131-a-bracket-the-lexer-found-open-in-a-type`. Symptom: `x =
# [1, 2` over `print(x)` cost the lexer's `unclosed_bracket`, and the lines
# below were read as the list's elements, since past an opener that never
# closes the lexer reads every line inside it, so `y = 3` below cost
# `expected_separator` at its `=`, and over `print(x)` alone the end of the
# block cost `expected_expression`. Now a literal whose opener the lexer
# found never closed ends at the first line end with no `,` before it, where
# its author ended it, and names no closer: the lexer's report is the one
# message (`selfhost/parse/unclosed.hero`).

function main()
    x = [1, 2  #~ unclosed_bracket
    y = 3
    print(x)
    print(y)
